摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"Bridge your pi extension, codex plugin or claude code plugin to dsh (DeepSeek Harness)","id":"gh:1336847233","install_available":true,"language":"TypeScript","name":"dsh-agents-plugins","slug":"openma-ai/dsh-agents-plugins","topics":["agent-plugin","agent-plugins","deepseek-harness","dsh-plugin","dsh-plugins"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Bridge your pi extension, codex plugin or claude code plugin to dsh (DeepSeek Harness)"},{"id":"p2s1","text":"dsh Agents Plugins Bridge"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"Install Agent Plugins, Codex plugins, Claude Code plugins, and Pi packages in\nDeepSeek Harness with "},{"id":"p3s2","text":"ns, Codex plugins, Claude Code plugins, and Pi packages in\nDeepSeek Harness with one bridge package."},{"id":"p4s1","text":"The Bridge is a normal DeepSeek Harness\nbundle: one install entry, many small Cordis plugins. It det"},{"id":"p4s2","text":"ects foreign package\nformats, copies an explicitly selected package into profile-local storage, and\n"},{"id":"p4s3","text":"materializes every supported capability as its own reversible DSH row. It does\nnot emulate another a"},{"id":"p4s4","text":"gent runtime or hide everything behind one universal\nplugin."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"## Quick start"},{"id":"p6s1","text":"Node.js 22.19 or newer is required. Install DSH first, then add the same Bridge\npackage to every pro"},{"id":"p6s2","text":"file that should use foreign plugins:"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"DSH profiles are separate compositions, so installing into `web` does not\nsilently mutate `tui`, and"},{"id":"p8s2","text":" vice versa. Users install only the root Bridge\npackage. It carries the Web surface, the format adap"},{"id":"p8s3","text":"ters, and MCP Apps support\nthrough its own dependency graph."},{"id":"p9s1","text":"### Web"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"Open **Settings → Plugins → Agent plugins** to scan local Codex, Claude Code,\nand Pi state; register"},{"id":"p10s2","text":" or import marketplaces; search catalogs; install a\nplugin; inspect per-plugin capability rows and d"},{"id":"p10s3","text":"iagnostics; and manage Pi\npackage update checks."},{"id":"p11s1","text":"The Web panel is a management surface over the Host runtime. Closing the panel\ndoes not stop install"},{"id":"p11s2","text":"ed hooks, commands, skills, MCP servers, or Pi extensions."},{"id":"p12s1","text":"### TUI"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"TUI does not need a second Bridge implementation. `/plugin-bridge`, imported\nslash commands, and use"},{"id":"p13s2","text":"r-invocable skills are projected from the same Host\ncomposition through ACP and appear in the TUI's "},{"id":"p13s3","text":"normal searchable command\nmenu. Hooks, monitors, MCP connections, agents, LSP rows, and Pi extension"},{"id":"p13s4","text":"\nlifecycle stay on the Host and continue to work without a browser."},{"id":"p14s1","text":"The screenshot comes from the\nDeepSeek Harness TUI, whose\ncommand menu is the surface Bridge command"},{"id":"p14s2","text":"s and imported skills join."},{"id":"p15s1","text":"MCP Apps are the intentional exception: the shared MCP connection, tools,\nresources, prompts, and ba"},{"id":"p15s2","text":"ckend hooks work in TUI, but untrusted App HTML is\nrendered only by the Web sandbox. The terminal do"},{"id":"p15s3","text":"es not execute browser UI."},{"id":"p16s1","text":"### Headless owner"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"Pi extensions such as `pi-telegram` may require one live Session even when no\nUI is open. Use\nMartty"},{"id":"p17s2","text":" owner\nfor that process lifecycle. Bridge still owns import, materialization, hooks,\ntools, commands"},{"id":"p17s3","text":", and extension runtime; Martty is the generic ACP `rpc` client\nthat keeps the Session alive and inv"},{"id":"p17s4","text":"okes only explicitly advertised startup\nand shutdown commands. It does not auto-approve permissions "},{"id":"p17s5","text":"or answer\nextension forms."},{"id":"p18s1","text":"| Capability | Web | TUI |\n|---|:---:|:---:|\n| Discover, import, install, enable, disable, uninstall"},{"id":"p18s2","text":" | panel + command | command |\n| Skills, slash commands, prompt templates | yes | yes |\n| Codex and "},{"id":"p18s3","text":"Claude Code hooks | yes | yes |\n| MCP tools, resources, prompts, and server lifecycle | yes | yes |\n"},{"id":"p18s4","text":"| Claude agents, output styles, monitors, and LSP | yes | yes |\n| Pi extensions, tools, commands, sk"},{"id":"p18s5","text":"ills, and lifecycle | yes | yes |\n| Foreign browser themes | yes | no |\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"## Architecture"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"The layout follows DSH's standard plugin shape:"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"Package-owned wrapper entries are important under pnpm: the profile resolves\nonly `@openma/dsh-agent"},{"id":"p22s2","text":"s-plugins-bridge/*`; each wrapper resolves its runtime\nfrom the Bridge package's own dependency grap"},{"id":"p22s3","text":"h, imports it through DSH's Loader,\nand mounts it as a child Cordis plugin. Transitive dependency ho"},{"id":"p22s4","text":"isting is never\npart of the runtime contract. Web-capable wrapper rows also expose their own\n`<row>/"},{"id":"p22s5","text":"package.json` plus an exact-id browser bundle, so DSH's official\n`dsh.client` scanner builds the Bro"},{"id":"p22s6","text":"wser tree from the same row instead of\nrequiring a second UI package in the profile."},{"id":"p23s1","text":"The lifecycle kernel exposes six reversible registries:"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"Every successful installation compiles to explicit rows. Each capability can\nload, fail, reload, dis"},{"id":"p25s2","text":"able, and uninstall independently. An MCP manifest\nexpands again so every configured server owns its"},{"id":"p25s3","text":" own\n`@deepseek-ai/dsh-mcp-client` row."},{"id":"p26s1","text":"MCP tools, resources, prompts, and Apps reuse one MCP SDK connection. The\nBridge includes the Host a"},{"id":"p26s2","text":"nd Web halves from\n`@openma/dsh-mcp-apps` through two\nindependent package-owned wrappers. A Codex re"},{"id":"p26s3","text":"gistered App is the foreign-host\nexception: its relay owns one Codex app-server process because Code"},{"id":"p26s4","text":"x still owns\nthat connection and OAuth lifecycle."},{"id":"p27s1","text":"Hook rows use the same dependency-wrapper pattern for DSH's official Codex and\nClaude Code hook plug"},{"id":"p27s2","text":"ins. The wrapper row owns the nested plugin fiber, so Web\nand TUI share one Host lifecycle without r"},{"id":"p27s3","text":"equiring the profile to install or\nhoist those runtime packages separately."},{"id":"p28s1","text":"## Compatibility"},{"id":"p29s1","text":"| Source | Catalog | Package | Materialized components |"},{"id":"p30s1","text":"| Agent Plugins 1.0 | marketplace dialect not standardized | `plugin.json` | `skills/`, `mcp.json` |"},{"id":"p30s2","text":"\n| Codex | `.agents/plugins/marketplace.json` | `.codex-plugin/plugin.json` | skills, MCP servers, r"},{"id":"p30s3","text":"egistered Apps, Codex hooks |\n| Claude Code | `.claude-plugin/marketplace.json` | `.claude-plugin/pl"},{"id":"p30s4","text":"ugin.json` | skills, MCP servers, hooks, commands, agents, output styles, monitors, themes, LSP serv"},{"id":"p30s5","text":"ers |\n| Pi | no marketplace registry | `package.json` with `pi`, or convention directories | extensi"},{"id":"p30s6","text":"ons, skills, prompt templates, themes |"},{"id":"p31s1","text":"Codex marketplace parsing follows the official OpenAI packaging reference: local sources may be a `."},{"id":"p31s2","text":"/` string or `{ \"source\": \"local\", \"path\": \"./...\" }`; HTTPS `url` and `git-subdir` entries honor `r"},{"id":"p31s3","text":"ef` or `sha`. Git subdirectories are copied from a root-contained path after clone. The documented `"},{"id":"p31s4","text":"npm` source is rejected with an explicit unsupported diagnostic because reproducing Codex's no-lifec"},{"id":"p31s5","text":"ycle-script install safely is not implemented yet."},{"id":"p32s1","text":"Claude marketplace-local directories plus the official `github`, HTTPS `url`, and `git-subdir` sourc"},{"id":"p32s2","text":"e shapes are supported. Git subdirectories must remain root-contained and `ref` or `sha` pins are pr"},{"id":"p32s3","text":"eserved. The documented `npm` source remains an explicit unsupported error; unknown source shapes ar"},{"id":"p32s4","text":"e never guessed or silently downgraded. GitHub marketplace URLs and `owner/repo@ref` shorthand are c"},{"id":"p32s5","text":"loned without a shell."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
